[h2]0.9.0 — Mining and progression[/h2]
[list]
[*]Scavenger Flags now mine Raw Deep Ore from visible outcrops. Workers haul it to Deep Drills; the invisible district ore pool is gone.
[*]Deep Drills consume 1 Raw Deep Ore + 3 Water to make 1 Deep Ore, using 1,000 hp. Their operating supplies are Metal Blocks and Treated Planks—not separately crafted drill bits. Help and status text now names the actual goods.
[*]The Stone Crusher can turn 3 Raw Deep Ore into 8 Dirt.
[*]Empty ore, sandstone and limestone outcrops remain and recover 20 units after five days. Recovery progress survives save/reload. Permanent mines and quarries remain the industrial supply.
[*]Deep Mines no longer require Deep Iron or Steel to build. Stone quarries now use only Planks, Treated Planks, Metal Blocks and Gears, preventing exhausted starter deposits from blocking permanent extraction.
[*]All 19 supported built-in maps receive authored mineral deposits on new-game creation. Existing settlements and custom maps get a one-time warning listing missing deposits; these maps are not automatically changed.
[*]All six mineral source types can be placed through the developer-mode map-object menu.
[/list]
[b]Existing saves:[/b] Remaining ore in old deposits is preserved as Raw Deep Ore. Processed ore in storage stays processed. Previously deleted outcrops cannot be restored automatically; use permanent seams or add replacements with developer tools. Supply your drills with raw ore, water, metal blocks and treated planks.
